WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.200
If you give up revenge,

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.600
are you saying the wrong didn’t matter?

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.560
Romans twelve tells us to leave vengeance

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.200
with God.

5
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.920
He sees what happened,

6
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.340
and he judges rightly.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.340
That’s a reason to trust him

8
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:15.960
with justice.

9
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.420
It isn’t a command to hide wrongdoing

10
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.820
or remain in danger.

11
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.440
In Romans thirteen,

12
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.780
Paul gives public authorities a role

13
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.100
in restraining evil.

14
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.760
Personal revenge and proper accountability are different.

15
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.300
You can tell the truth,

16
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.520
seek protection,

17
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.560
and ask for help without trying

18
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.440
to make them suffer.

19
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.980
The God who showed you mercy takes

20
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.220
evil seriously.

21
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.920
Bring him your anger,

22
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.000
and take the next honest step.

23
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.600
You can seek what’s right while entrusting

24
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.960
final judgment to him.
